(251, 9, '2004-05-29 16:13:38', '2004-05-29 21:13:38', '<a href=''http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/articles/wp-content/uploads/2007/05/off_road_step85.jpg'' title=''off_road_step85.jpg''><img src=''http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/articles/wp-content/uploads/2007/05/off_road_step85.jpg'' alt=''off_road_step85.jpg'' /></a>\r\n\r\n<!--more-->\r\n\r\nHere are a couple of pics of a jump ramp I made recently. The base is made of corrugated cardboard and it''s all held together with pva glue. I''ve added a couple of supports to stiffen it up, but it''s probably not necessary. For the top I used some thin cardboard and I put some foam rubber pads on the rear underneath to stop it slipping. Craploads of cheap fun!!\r\n\r\nAnd here''s some of the fun just waiting for you when you''re done! You''ll find more jump action pics in my ramp action gallery.\r\n\r\n<a href=''http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/articles/wp-content/uploads/2007/05/off_road_step86.jpg'' title=''off_road_step86.jpg''><img src=''http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/articles/wp-content/uploads/2007/05/off_road_step86.jpg'' alt=''off_road_step86.jpg'' /></a>\r\n\r\n<a href="http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/articles/2004/05/30/off-road-bits-part-10-skid-pans/">Next: Off-Road Bits - Part 10: Skid Pans</a>', 'Off-Road Bits - Part 9: Ramps', 0, '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'off-road-bits-part-9-ramps', '', '', '2008-01-10 18:38:19', '2008-01-11 00:38:19', '', 0, 'http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/articles/2004/05/29/off-road-bits-part-9-ramps/', 0, 'post', '', 0),
